      "side": 1,
      "message": "At Pathset 2 this isn\u0027t complete (still need to modify the ports that don\u0027t compile on Linux) but I think this is a kind of thing I\u0027d like to do. The initial motivation for this was to allow a glyph to decide if it has a path or not depending on if that path will actually be used to draw it. (So that COLRv0 and COLRv1 glyphs don\u0027t try to pretend they can be drawn from a path resulting in bad behavior when stroking or emboldening is requested.) Along the way this also fixes up a few other edge cases and also propagates up the stack that a glyph path is a dev-path not a user-path, so it needs an extra \u0027hairline\u0027 property so we know if its a fill path or not.",
      "revId": "4ff3dcff273f9aebcafbc1e52ae2d13012370548",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
